{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfbYvRAedhWwSEWSRP1BG", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Put it in a **new migration file, `migrations/0008_add_customer_phone.sql`**. Don't edit `0007_add_customers.sql`.\n\nThe project's memory store has a rule that files in `migrations/` have already been applied in production. They must never be edited; every change gets a new file with the next 4-digit number. The newest one now is `0007`, so yours is `0008`:\n\n```sql\nALTER TABLE customers ADD COLUMN phone TEXT;\n```\n\nI made it nullable because existing customer rows have no phone number. If you need `NOT NULL`, you'll have to give it a default or backfill those rows first.\n\nSeparately, `0007_add_customers.sql` creates a column misspelled as `emial`, not `email`. If you want to fix that, it also has to be a new migration (`RENAME COLUMN`), not an edit to `0007`. You could do it in the same `0008` file or a separate one, and any code that reads that column would need updating too.\n\nI haven't created the file. Say if you want me to."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 641, "cache_read_input_tokens": 22309, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 641}, "output_tokens": 5, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "d94a5312-2542-4bad-9797-262daebadcac", "uuid": "3f3d8cc8-100a-4755-b425-f39895d6f8a9", "timestamp": "2026-10-01T12:54:17.424Z", "request_id": "req_011CfbYvQq4Abe9HM1Veo9Ci"}
